# Who must review a change, when the repository's branch protection rule says
# code owners are required.
#
# `.github/` is the folder that decides what runs with this repository's secrets:
# a workflow file chooses its triggers, its permissions and the token it hands a
# job. Requiring the owner's review here means a pull request cannot merge its own
# workflow change, which is the merge-time half of the rule the workflows
# themselves enforce at run time.
#
# This file is inside the pattern on purpose: a change to who reviews workflow
# changes needs the same review it demands of everything else.
/.github/ @goFrendiAsgard
